# =============================================================================
# CODEOWNERS — Review Ownership Model
# =============================================================================
#
# PURPOSE
# -------
# This file tells GitHub which reviewers to auto-request when a pull request
# touches each path.  At least one CODEOWNER must approve before a PR can be
# merged (requires "Require review from Code Owners" in branch protection).
#
# OWNERSHIP TIERS
# ---------------
# 1. DEFAULT (@dark-sarge)
#    Catches everything not covered by a more-specific rule below.
#    This is the repository maintainer.
#
# 2. CONTRACTS REVIEWERS (@airflex-org/contracts-reviewers + @dark-sarge)
#    Any change to the Soroban smart contracts must be reviewed by at least
#    one member of the contracts-reviewers team in addition to the maintainer.
#    Smart contracts handle real user funds; on-chain changes are irreversible.
#    Replace @airflex-org/contracts-reviewers with your actual GitHub org team.
#
# 3. SECURITY REVIEWERS (@airflex-org/security-reviewers + @dark-sarge)
#    Authentication middleware and core business-logic services are attack
#    surfaces.  Changes require a security-aware reviewer in addition to the
#    maintainer.  Replace @airflex-org/security-reviewers with your actual team.
#
# 4. DEVOPS REVIEWERS (@airflex-org/devops + @dark-sarge)
#    CI/CD pipeline changes can bypass security controls or leak secrets.
#    All workflow and GitHub configuration changes require DevOps sign-off.
#    Replace @airflex-org/devops with your actual team.
#
# BOT EXEMPTIONS
# --------------
# Dependabot opens PRs as dependabot[bot]; GitHub automatically waives
# CODEOWNER review requirements for bot-opened PRs when the repository's
# branch-protection rule allows it.  No special entries are needed here —
# bot PRs are handled by the dependabot-auto-merge workflow instead.
#
# TESTING THIS FILE
# -----------------
# Open a draft PR that touches a file in each protected path and confirm that
# GitHub auto-requests the correct reviewer(s) in the "Reviewers" sidebar.
# Paths to test:
#   contracts/escrow/src/lib.rs      → should request contracts-reviewers + dark-sarge
#   server/src/middleware/auth*.ts   → should request security-reviewers + dark-sarge
#   server/src/services/stellar.ts  → should request security-reviewers + dark-sarge
#   .github/workflows/ci.yml        → should request devops + dark-sarge
#
# SYNTAX REFERENCE
# ----------------
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
# Rules are evaluated last-match-wins; more-specific patterns below override
# the catch-all at the top.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Default owner — catches everything not matched by a more-specific rule
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                       @dark-sarge

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Smart contracts
#    Any change under contracts/ requires both the maintainer AND a member of
#    the contracts-reviewers team.  On-chain logic, escrow mechanics, and
#    deployment configuration all live here.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
contracts/                              @dark-sarge @airflex-org/contracts-reviewers

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Backend authentication & security-critical services
#    Middleware handles JWT validation, RBAC, rate-limiting, and request
#    validation.  Services include fraud detection, wallet logic, and Stellar
#    integration.  Both paths require a security reviewer.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
server/src/middleware/                  @dark-sarge @airflex-org/security-reviewers
server/src/services/                    @dark-sarge @airflex-org/security-reviewers

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. CI/CD pipelines and GitHub configuration
#    Workflow files can exfiltrate secrets, bypass required checks, or alter
#    deployment targets.  All .github/ changes require DevOps approval.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.github/                                @dark-sarge @airflex-org/devops

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Frontend
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
frontend/                               @dark-sarge

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Docs site
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
apps/docs-site/                         @dark-sarge
docs/                                   @dark-sarge
*.md                                    @dark-sarge
